[{"id":"VRCE-7-58-1","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":58,"verse":1,"english":"On the same night ſatrughna housed himself in a thatched cottage Sitā gave birth to twin sons.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.758,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-66-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7058001","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"77b7e3a3ead33d38226b0a7249cd31e016a9e64a1228417e2ea6375bbd3ff1cd","compact":"93c9fd7ea82a996611df856066751a2b1cf44d7737d02cc2837c30faab3e67e8","nasal":"93c9fd7ea82a996611df856066751a2b1cf44d7737d02cc2837c30faab3e67e8"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-58-2","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":58,"verse":2,"english":"In the midnight the Muni boys came to Vālmīki and communicated to him this auspicious intelligence, saying. “O illustrious Sir, the beloved spouse of Rāma has given birth to two sons; do you so protect them that evil spirits not injure them.\"","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.804,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-66-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7058002","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"96042328e86d5e48b0e0f0c1f7f89fe3cae33d9dd9b66986beac183d9c580717","compact":"5b72e85be85e4a6dc0877d672c8cf6023e38888c1349de0c8e528bfbc57816da","nasal":"5b72e85be85e4a6dc0877d672c8cf6023e38888c1349de0c8e528bfbc57816da"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-58-3","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":58,"verse":3,"english":"Hearing those words the highly effulgent Vālmīki went there and attained to great on beholding those two highly effulgent sons, resembling the newly risen sun and the celestials. Thereupon he made arrangements against the oppression of ghosts and goblins.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.581,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-66-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7058003","sanskritFile":"Ram0